  <string name="audio_adv_auto_preamp">Automatic preamp</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_auto_preamp_idle">Lowers the volume as much as the curve boosts, to avoid distortion</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_auto_preamp_lowers">Lowers %1$s dB so the boosts do not distort</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_back">Audio</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_balance">Balance</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_bass_freq">Bass frequency</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_correction_auto_footer">The correction chosen with headphones connected is saved for them and comes back by itself when they reconnect. On the speaker, no correction, unless you choose one while it plays. Wired headphones are treated as one, because the connector does not report the model.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_correction_manual_footer">The chosen correction stays the same on any output.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_crossfade">Crossfade</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_crossfade_footer">Consecutive tracks of the same album change with no gap and no crossfade, so the album sounds whole. There is also no crossfade on tracks shorter than twice the chosen duration, with Repeat one, with T.A.R.K.A.S. Spatial on, or when there is narrated curiosity. Pausing, dragging the bar or skipping during the transition ends the crossfade at once.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_crossfade_off">Off: songs change with no gap and no overlap</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_crossfade_on">The next song comes in while the current one goes out, over %1$d s</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_crossfade_spatial">With T.A.R.K.A.S. Spatial on, songs change without crossfade: the spatial effect follows one song at a time.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_device_reduces">The headphone correction already lowers %1$s dB to avoid distortion.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_dump_apps">To see which apps are playing, grant the DUMP permission once. Android only grants it from a computer, with this command. It is how ADB mode finds the other apps to equalize.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_dump_missing">DUMP permission missing</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_dump_steps">Turn on USB debugging, connect the phone to the computer and run the command once. Until then, only players that announce their own audio session are equalized.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_duration">Duration</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_group_engineering">Engineering</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_group_playback">Playback</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_group_sound">Sound</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_limiter_ceiling">Limiter ceiling</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_limiter_sub">Prevents distortion when the curve adds too much gain</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_limits_app">Without root, the equalizer processes only what T.A.R.K.A.S. plays. For other apps, choose ADB or root in Reach.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_limits_other">In other apps, the headphone correction, the bands, bass, treble, preamp, limiter and, on Android 9 or later, the balance apply. Stereo width and virtualizer apply only to what T.A.R.K.A.S. plays. Some protected apps (calls, DRM) may refuse the effect. To follow the curve down to the bass, the sound of other apps comes out about 85 ms late: in videos, the voice may be slightly out of sync.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_album">By album</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_album_sub">Keeps the difference between the tracks of an album, when the file carries the album value</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_applied">Applied adjustment</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_auto">Automatic</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_auto_sub">By album when an album plays in order; by track otherwise</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_current">Current track</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_footer">Evens songs out at −14 LUFS. It only lowers the volume, never raises it, to avoid distortion. It uses the file\'s ReplayGain value, if any. Without it, it measures the song while it plays and applies the result from the next time. The measurement only counts if the song plays almost entirely.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_measuring">Measuring during this playback</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_off">Off</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_src_album">album tag</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_src_measured">measured</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_src_track">track tag</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_track">By track</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_loudness_track_sub">All songs at the same volume</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_meter_active">Active</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_meter_footer">Experimental. Measures the volume of audio played by other apps, using Android audio capture (10 or later). Apps that block capture do not appear. It does not equalize them and does not identify the song. It turns off by itself when you leave this page.</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_meter_inactive">Inactive</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_meter_start">Turn the meter on</string>
  <string name="audio_adv_meter_stop">Turn the meter off</string>
